e":"text","text":"In a DOM Range object, the startContainer + startOffset tuple represents the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"type":"text","text":" boundary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point. Similarly, the the endContainer + endOffset tuple represents the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"type":"text","text":" boundary point."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In both cases, the start\/endContainer property is a pointer to either a DOM text node, or a DOM"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element (this typically depends on the mechanism from which the DOM Range instance originates,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for example when obtaining the currently-selected document fragment using the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"window.selection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API). In the case of a DOM text node, the start\/endOffset corresponds to a position within the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"character data. In the case of a DOM element node, the start\/endOffset corresponds to a position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that designates a child text node."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"type":"text","text":" field is optional. When only the start field is specified, the domRange object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"represents a “collapsed” range that has identical "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"type":"text","text":" boundary points."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"https:\/\/github.com\/readium\/architecture\/blob\/master\/models\/locators\/extensions\/html.md#the-domrange-object"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/readiumshared\/domrange"]}